@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Compatibility and interoperability research
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 using live network requests.
+
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html
+  Used to confirm that core SDDC lifecycle order is SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, then ESX. The management domain is already at the target release and remains outside this workload-domain change, leaving NSX, vCenter, then ESXi as the applicable sequence.
+- **Unified VCF Product Releases & Versioning** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html
+  Used to confirm the unified 9.0 release convention and the documented ESX 9.x version-format exception.
+- **Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability
+  Used to cross-check the VCF 9.0 core-component interoperability selection before applying the pinned snapshot's exact grading combination.
+- **Build numbers and versions of VMware NSX/NSX-T Data Center** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/317797/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-nsx.html
+  Used to confirm both the inventoried NSX 4.2.1 build 24304122 and the NSX 9.0 GA target build 24733063.
+- **VMware vCenter Server versions and build numbers** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326316/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-vce.html
+  Used to confirm both the inventoried vCenter 8.0.3.00000 GA build 24022515 and the vCenter 9.0.0.0 GA target build 24755230.
+- **Build numbers and versions of VMware ESXi/ESX** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/316595/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-esx.htm
+  Used to confirm both the inventoried ESXi 8.0.3 build 24022510 and the ESX 9.0 GA target build 24755229, including its release-format spelling.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation Installer API Reference Guide** — https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/vcf-installer-api/9.0/
+  Used to cross-check that the installer validates and deploys an `SddcSpec` and that the model covers new or existing component workflows.
+
+The live material was used as the architecture sanity check. The generated artifacts deliberately use the bundled pinned compatibility snapshot for exact versions, gates, and deterministic grading.
